    "['ipv6 pim sparse-mode', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols pim interface <interface-name> family inet6 mode sparse-dense', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ipv6 pim sparse-mode` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols pim interface <interface-name> family inet6 mode sparse-dense\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In Juniper, you need to specify the interface name where PIM should be enabled\\n2. The command includes `family inet6` to specify IPv6 operation\\n3. Juniper uses \"sparse-dense\" mode which is functionally equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"sparse-mode\" in most implementations (Juniper doesn\\'t have a pure sparse-mode option)\\n\\nFor example, for interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0, the full command would be:\\n`set protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0 family inet6 mode sparse-dense`', 'trans_template': 'set protocols pim interface <interface-name> family inet6 mode sparse-dense'}]]": 1,
    "['ipv6 pim sparse-mode', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols pim interface all mode sparse', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols pim interface all mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent enables PIM sparse mode globally. If you need interface-specific configuration (more precise translation of the Cisco command), it would be:\\n##\\nset protocols pim interface <interface-name> mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nFor the exact translation of the Cisco configuration, you would need to specify each interface separately in Juniper, like:\\n##\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/1 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/2 mode sparse\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols pim interface all mode sparse'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols pim interface <interface-name> mode sparse', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols pim interface all mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent enables PIM sparse mode globally. If you need interface-specific configuration (more precise translation of the Cisco command), it would be:\\n##\\nset protocols pim interface <interface-name> mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nFor the exact translation of the Cisco configuration, you would need to specify each interface separately in Juniper, like:\\n##\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/1 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/2 mode sparse\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols pim interface <interface-name> mode sparse'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0 mode sparse', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '#